body:
## Scope

Completes Issue #20 queue tasks 191–200 as a stacked draft on PR #67.

## Academy

- limits public Academy programs to U.S. Logistics Operations and Marketing;
- keeps the existing interactive five-screen flow and six capability layers;
- reclassifies the AI assistant lab as an optional Marketing exercise, not a third program;
- separates paid cohorts from free practice opportunities;
- publishes no fixed Academy price and accepts no Academy payment;
- adds explicit no-guarantee boundaries for employment, income, clients, certification, promotion, access, and future work;
- overrides Academy metadata and Service schema to the two approved public programs.

## Careers

- adds a central current-vacancy status panel to `/logistics/careers/`;
- keeps general professional-interest inquiries open for manual review;
- verified public vacancy registry is empty;
- emits no JobPosting schema when no role is verified open;
- defines the required owner approval, employment type, location, source, review-date, and expiry gates for future JobPosting use;
- adds privacy and no-employment-guarantee boundaries.

## Monitoring and release governance

- Search Console watchlist entries for pending digital-service, niche-service, Academy, and Careers releases;
- all pending metrics remain null and inspection status remains `not_requested` until owner-approved merge, deploy, and live verification;
- weekly and monthly growth scorecards;
- final readiness checklist covering privacy, claims, SEO, contact routing, latest-head CI, owner merge/deploy approval, and dated measurement.

## Data and approval boundary

- no real applicant, employee, customer, carrier, shipment, or OFFICE 374 data;
- no identity documents, credentials, financial information, salaries, commissions, benefits, schedules, or country eligibility invented;
- no payment, enrollment, employment, interview, training access, team placement, contract, compensation, or future-work guarantee;
- no merge, deployment, DNS, Cloudflare, billing, account, credential, deletion, or public communication action.

## Verification

GitHub Actions must pass:

1. `npm run build`
2. `npm test`
3. `npm run test:e2e`

This PR is stacked on `seo/niche-seo-services-185-188` and may be retargeted only after the base stack is owner-approved and merged.

Related: #20 and draft PR #19.
